  "all_ingredients_flat": "millet flour, rag, finger millet, bajra, pearl millet, jowar, sorghum, besan, chickpea flour, flax, oats, chia seeds, hemp heart, baking powder, baking soda, water, ACV, Apple Cider Vinegar, whole psyllium husks, isabgol, dates, Italian herb mix, Jeera, cumin seeds, crushed walnuts, nuts, seeds, minced garlic, jalapenos",
  "instructions": "Gluten-Free Bread is dense in texture. Takes 15 minutes for prep and then 2 hours to bake. Lasts 1 week in my fridge.\n*   BATTER: Mix water, vinegar and isabgol (psyllium husks). Set aside for 5 mins. Mix the rest of the ingredients (dry ingredients) in a bowl thoroughly. Then add the isabgol, water & vinegar mix.\n*   BAKING PAN: For oil-free preparation, use a non-stick baking pan. I prefer to use a glass baking pan with 1/4 tsp oil to coat the entire baking dish. I use a brush to ensure even coating.\n*   BAKING: Pour the batter into the baking pan. I score the middle and lower the height so that after baking, the top is more even in height. Set oven on bake (no convection) at 325 F. Bake for 120 mins. You may need to experiment with the settings depending on oven.\n*   SLICING & TOASTING: Let cool before slicing. The bread may be a little damp when we slice it, but it comes out right upon toasting. I toast each slice for about 9 minutes at 425 F.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "bake",
    "toast"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "Let cool before slicing. The bread may be a little damp when we slice it, but it comes out right upon toasting. I toast each slice for about 9 minutes at 425 F.",
  "notes": "Optional - have fun playing with different combinations!\nGluten-Free Bread is dense in texture. Takes 15 minutes for prep and then 2 hours to bake. Lasts 1 week in my fridge.\nA recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (millet flour), BEANS (chickpea flour), NUTS & SEEDS (flax, chia, hemp hearts), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (ACV), SWEETENER (dates), MISC (baking powder, ...).",
